## Scope

```js
function test() {
  if (true) {
    var v = 'function scoped';  // accessible outside the if block
    let l = 'block scoped';    // only inside this block
  }
  console.log(v); // 'function scoped'
  console.log(l); // ReferenceError
}
```

## Hoisting

```js
console.log(v); // undefined — var hoisted & initialised
console.log(l); // ReferenceError — let in TDZ
var v = 1;
let l = 2;
```

## Re-declaration

```js
var x = 1;
var x = 2; // silent, fine

let y = 1;
let y = 2; // SyntaxError
```

## Loop variable leakage (classic bug)

```js
// var leaks out and captures the final value:
for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
// prints: 3 3 3

// let creates a fresh binding per iteration:
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
// prints: 0 1 2
```

