## Shorter syntax

```js
// Traditional
const double = function(x) { return x * 2; };

// Arrow — one-liner with implicit return
const double = x => x * 2;

// Multi-line arrow still needs explicit return
const greet = (name) => {
  const msg = `Hello, ${name}`;
  return msg;
};
```

## Lexical this — the main reason they exist

```js
class Timer {
  constructor() { this.seconds = 0; }

  start() {
    // Without arrow: 'this' inside setTimeout is undefined (strict) or window
    setInterval(function() { this.seconds++; }, 1000); // BROKEN

    // With arrow: 'this' is the Timer instance
    setInterval(() => { this.seconds++; }, 1000);      // ✅
  }
}
```

## Array method callbacks

```js
const nums = [1, 2, 3];
const doubled = nums.map(n => n * 2);         // [2, 4, 6]
const evens   = nums.filter(n => n % 2 === 0); // [2]
```

## When NOT to use

```js
const obj = {
  name: 'Aaron',
  // Arrow captures 'this' from module scope, not the object:
  greet: () => console.log(this?.name), // undefined
  // Regular method — correct:
  greet() { console.log(this.name); }   // 'Aaron'
};
```

